  "name": "Question 2",
  "problem": "Find \n$|\\begin{aligned}-3 & b & 0 \\\\ d & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -4\\end{aligned}|$\ngiven that \n$|\\begin{aligned}-3 & b \\\\ d & 2\\end{aligned}|=-7.$",
  "worked_solution": "Notice that we have a block diagonal matrix. Therefore, its determinant is equal to the product of the diagonal blocks' determinants:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}-3 & b & 0 \\\\ d & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -4\\end{aligned}| & =|\\begin{aligned}-3 & b & 0 \\\\ d & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}-3 & b \\\\ d & 2\\end{aligned}|\\cdot (-4) \\\\  & =(-7)\\cdot (-4) \\\\  & =28.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
